{% for agent in agents %}
{% if agent.featured %}
<article class="agent-profile">
  <p class="agent-role">{{ agent.role }}</p>
  <h2 id="{{ agent.id }}">{{ agent.name }} <a class="heading-anchor" href="#{{ agent.id }}" aria-label="Permalink to {{ agent.name }}">#</a></h2>
  {% for paragraph in agent.paragraphs %}
  <p>{{ paragraph }}</p>
  {% endfor %}
  <p class="agent-ask"><strong>Ask about:</strong> {{ agent.consult }}</p>
  <p class="agent-source">
    <a href="{{ agent.repo }}">{{ agent.repoName }}</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
    entry <code>{{ agent.entry }}</code>
  </p>
</article>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<section class="agent-roster-section" aria-labelledby="roster-title">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 id="roster-title">More of the crew</h2>
    <p>The page is built to hold the whole series. As each new agent is finished, it appears here with its own voice, repository and audit.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="agent-roster">
    {% for agent in agents %}
    {% if not agent.featured %}
    <article class="agent-roster-item" id="{{ agent.id }}">
      <p class="agent-role">{{ agent.role }}</p>
      <h3>{{ agent.name }} <a class="heading-anchor" href="#{{ agent.id }}" aria-label="Permalink to {{ agent.name }}">#</a></h3>
      <p>{{ agent.short or agent.paragraphs[0] }}</p>
      <p class="agent-ask"><strong>Ask about:</strong> {{ agent.consult }}</p>
      <p class="agent-source"><a href="{{ agent.repo }}">{{ agent.repoName }}</a></p>
    </article>
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  {% if agents | length <= 2 %}
  <p class="roster-empty">The next agents are still being written. When they are ready, they will join the roster here.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<h2 id="shared-archive">Same archive, separate lives</h2>

Each agent has its own repository, entry file, private memory and audit. Neither
agent imports the other's files. What they share is the Grimoire, reached through
a `lore/` link or clone.

That separation is on purpose. One agent's private notes and voice should not leak
into the other, and either agent should be deployable on its own.

<h2 id="asking-a-friend">Asking a friend</h2>

They can still work together. `series/agents.json` lists the agents in the series.
Deployment reads that list and installs two things per agent: the main entry, and
a read-only consult copy.

A main agent can ask a peer's consult copy a question. The copy can read the
Grimoire and answer in character, but it cannot edit files, run shell commands,
read the peer's private folder or ask someone else. Its reply is lore to think
about, not instructions to follow.

